------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications by Foodini
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Per Apache-2.0 section 4(b), files changed by Foodini carry a notice
saying so. The substantive changes from the fork point are:

  * Reduced to the Python binding. The R, Rust, C++ and MATLAB bindings
    and their conformance checkers were removed. The catalog schema
    (schema/catalog.sql) and the conformance corpus (conformance/) are
    retained unchanged.
  * Removed the original author's blog/ directory. That material is his
    writing about his project and is not ours to republish.
  * Moved the Python package from py/okf to src/okf.
  * Renamed the distribution from "okf-ingest" to "foodini-okf-ingest",
    and the console script from "okf" to "okf-ingest".
  * Raised the minimum Python version from 3.9 to 3.14; the project is
    uv-managed.
  * Rewrote the documentation that described the multi-binding design,
    and updated the self-documenting bundle in docs/okf-bundle
    accordingly.

